              <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{0},r_{0}\leftarrow l_{s},r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{0},r_{0}\leftarrow l_{s},r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize thresholds
<span id="alg2.l5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> 1. Find the tightest <math id="alg2.l5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg2.l5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
